      "writtenOn": "2024-01-09T08:10:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u0027Product\u0027 read `PRODUCT_PRODCT_VNDK_VERSION` which is removed and assumed to be `current` now. As the value is assumed to be current, it reads `PLATFORM_VNDK_VERSION`, which is the same as the vendor case of `BOARD_VNDK_VERSION \u003d\u003d current`. (please refer to this change: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/2762829/1/cc/genrule.go).\n\nNow, the `BOARD_VNDK_VERSION`, although it is for vendor, is the only switch to turn on/off the vndk definition, I think it is reasonable to use the same switch for both cases.",
      "parentUuid": "0406b5a6_fda7e271",
